# Focus

> A tiny, even C++ interface for an AI model. Header-only.

## Purpose
Explain focus as the thin door every model is asked to walk through. Source: fitzyracing1/focus.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Include the header.
2. Talk to any model through the same small door.
3. Do not grow a framework.
4. Keep the page and the header together in the source.

## Key ideas
- Header-only (you include a file; you do not link a large library)
- Uniform interface (every model sees the same door)
- Minimal (few calls on purpose)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/focus
#include "focus.hpp"
model.ask(input)
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. #include "focus.hpp" → “bring in the thin door”
2. model.ask(input) → “send one question through that door”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a new model appears → it must use this same door
- If a call is not on the door → it does not belong in focus

## What a person would notice
One small header instead of a stack of tools.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open the header in fitzyracing1/focus.
